Subject: [PATCH] 5321: accepting a message runs on its own database lane
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tester's 200-seat re-run after 0349: every run answered, but a send still
took 14.6 s to be accepted — its few lookups queued behind 200 runs' in the
short pool (40, 0 idle, ~550 waiting). Requests to POST /threads/:id/message
now enter an AsyncLocalStorage „intake lane" before the sign-in check, and
ordinary-timeout queries made on it draw from a pool of their own (10). The
run the send starts leaves the lane, back on the ordinary pools.

